The following binary search is called with `arr` = `{1, 8, 9, 10, 20, 23, 25, 28, 37, 47, 53, 58}` and `target` = 43.

```java
int low = 0, high = arr.length - 1;
while (low <= high) {
    int mid = (low + high) / 2;
    if (arr[mid] == target) {
        return mid;
    }
    if (arr[mid] < target) {
        low = mid + 1;
    } else {
        high = mid - 1;
    }
}
return -1;
```

Which values of `arr[mid]` are compared with the target, in order?

